# machine translation from Hungarian, not reviewed yet
#: ../src/main.cpp
msgid "A new color picking feature has been added, and on purpose it is not bound to any key.\\nIt lets you pick the color for the selected lines from the video at the mouse position with a single keypress.\\n\\nPressed twice quickly it restores the first write and magnifies that part of the video around the pointer. The popup lets you select an exact pixel and optionally write the accepted color in the dynamic \\t(<current millisecond>,<current millisecond>,\\c...) form.\\n\\nFrom that magnified view you can also read the color along a Mocha motion track held on the clipboard, including its position, scale and rotation, which writes the color the tracked point passes over as a sequence of \\t() tags.\\n\\nTo use it, assign the \"video/colorpick/primary|outline|shadow\" commands to hotkeys (one key each is recommended)."
msgstr "Kolore-hautatzaile berria gehitu da; nahita ez zaio automatikoki esleitu inolako botoiri.\\nHaren bidez, hautatutako lerroen kolorea saguaren azpiko bideoko pixelaren kolorearekin ordez dezakezu botoi bat sakatuta.\\n\\nBi aldiz azkar sakatzean, lehen kolore-sarrera berrezartzen du eta saguaren inguruko bideo-zatia handitzen du. Laster-leihoan pixel zehatza hauta dezakezu, eta onartutako kolorea nahi izanez gero dinamikoa \\t(<uneko milisegundoa>,<uneko milisegundoa>,\\c...) formatuan sar dezakezu.\\n\\nHanditutako ikuspegian, kolorea arbelean dagoen Mocha motion track baten ibilbidean ere irakur dezakezu, haren posizioa, eskala eta biraketa kontuan hartuta. Kasu horretan, programak jarraitutako puntuaren azpiko kolorea \\t() etiketa-segida gisa sartzen du.\\n\\nErabiltzeko, esleitu \"video/colorpick/primary|outline|shadow\" komandoak laster-teklei (bakoitzari botoi bana gomendatzen zaio)."

